Task ID: nrf_l2_002
Category: network_routing_forwarding
Difficulty: level_2

Original Instruction:
Write an XDP program that performs next-hop routing. Look up the IPv4 destination address. If destination IP is 10.0.2.1, rewrite destination MAC to next-hop gateway and return XDP_TX. Otherwise return XDP_PASS.

Technical Requirements:
- Match IPv4 packets with destination IP 10.0.2.1
- Rewrite eth->h_dest and return XDP_TX on match
- Pass all other traffic with XDP_PASS
- Check boundaries on Ethernet and IPv4 headers

Previous Implementation:
```c
#include <linux/bpf.h>
#include <linux/if_ether.h>
#include <linux/ip.h>
#include <linux/ipv6.h>
#include <linux/tcp.h>
#include <linux/udp.h>
#include <linux/icmp.h>
#include <linux/in.h>
